+## Handshake and visibility
+
+- Every ready/valid decision uses pre-edge state. `rst` or `cancel` drives
+  `in_meta_ready`, `in_ready`, `out_meta_valid` and `out_valid` low and
+  suppresses every transfer on that edge. Reset has priority over cancel.
+- Admission is `in_meta_ready iff !faulted && !receiving && level < 2` on the
+  old state. A simultaneous retire does not create credit when old `level == 2`;
+  the resulting one-cycle full-queue bubble is intentional.
+- One accepted descriptor immediately reserves the tail slot and increments
+  `level` and `stat_meta`. Only one input payload can be open.
+- No input-to-output same-edge bypass, no descriptor-to-first-payload
+  acceptance, and no output-metadata-to-first-output-byte delivery.
+- A success frame becomes visible only after its final accepted payload byte
+  seals it. Its metadata handshake precedes its payload. An upstream-error
+  frame retires on its metadata handshake and never emits payload.
+- `out_last` is generated from the sealed byte length. Metadata and payload
+  remain stable while their valid is asserted and ready is low. Frames do not
+  interleave. Duplicate tags are legal and are not slot identities.
+
+## Framing and faults
+
+- `in_meta_error == 0`: legal only for `bytes` in 1..256 and
+  `8*(bytes-1) < valid_bits <= 8*bytes`, computed with sufficient unsigned
+  width. The descriptor fields are stored and transported unchanged.
+- `in_meta_error != 0`: legal only with `bytes == 0` and `valid_bits == 0`.
+  The descriptor is sealed immediately and forwarded unchanged with no payload.
+  Code 3 is accepted as an opaque injected code; this queue assigns it no
+  producer or public meaning.
+- Any other descriptor reserves a slot but poisons it, latches `faulted`,
+  pulses `fault_event` once, sets `fault_code=1`, and increments `stat_fault`
+  once. The poisoned slot is never exposed and no payload is accepted for it.
+- Each accepted payload byte increments `stat_in_bytes`, including an offending
+  byte. At accepted index `i`, `in_last` must equal `(i == bytes-1)`. An early
+  last or a missing last at the declared final byte poisons the reservation,
+  sets `fault_code=2`, and increments `stat_fault` once. Accepted indices are
+  always 0..255; there is no out-of-bounds write, implicit drain or guessed
+  re-synchronization.
+- `faulted` is sticky until reset/cancel and disables only new input. Older
+  sealed frames may still drain in order. The poisoned reservation is retained
+  until explicit cancellation. Silence is not a timeout.
+- Cancel gates all ready/valid low on its edge, discards every allocated slot
+  (sealed, partially output, partial input or poisoned), adds the pre-edge
+  `level` to `stat_aborted` with saturation, preserves the other counters, and
+  clears local fault/control state. Held cancel cannot count an old slot twice.
+  Reset clears data-flow control and all counters.
+- Counters saturate at `2**STAT_W - 1` and never affect data flow. Before
+  saturation and between resets,
+  `stat_meta == stat_retired + stat_aborted + level`.
+
